cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "OcuTrace: browser-based nystagmus and saccade recording from phone video"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype that turns a phone video of the eyes into a quantitative
  oculomotor recording. Tracks the iris and a fixed facial reference point in
  the browser, runs a standardized task battery (fixation, gaze holding,
  prosaccades, antisaccades, smooth pursuit, optokinetic and positional
  testing) aligned by audio start tones, and reports per-task measures with
  raw traces, a recording quality check and Eye-Tracking-BIDS export. Not a
  medical device and not for diagnosis.
